[{"category":"section","location":"examples/#Examples","page":"Examples","text":"using ELFINData\nusing Dates\nusing ELFINData.DimensionalData\nusing SpacePhysicsMakie, WGLMakie\n\n# https://data.elfin.ucla.edu/ela/overplots/2022/09/05/ela_l2_overview_20220905_10_ndes.gif\nt0 = DateTime(\"2022-09-05T10:00:00\")\nt1 = DateTime(\"2022-09-05T10:30:00\")\n\nspectra = epd_spectral(t0, t1; probe = \"ela\")[Ti(t0 .. t1)]\ntplot([spectra.omni, spectra.anti, spectra.perp, spectra.para]; colormap=:turbo)\nFigureAxes()","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"validation/#Validation-and-Benchmark-with-PySPEDAS","page":"Validation and Benchmark","text":"We compare ELFINData results against PySPEDAS to ensure numerical parity and to track performance. The following benchmarks illustrate the typical workflow.\n\nState variable ELA_POS_GEI: Julia is about 200 times faster than Python for this retrieval.\n\nusing PySPEDAS\nusing ELFINData\nusing Chairmarks\n\ntrange = (\"2021-08-08\", \"2021-08-10\")\nela_pos_gei = getdata(ELA_POS_GEI, trange)\npy_ela_pos_gei = Array(PySPEDAS.elfin.state(trange).ela_pos_gei)\n@assert ela_pos_gei == py_ela_pos_gei'\n@b Array(getdata(ELA_POS_GEI, trange)), PySPEDAS.elfin.state(trange), pyspedas.projects.elfin.state(trange)\n(36.300 ms (903 allocs: 8.076 MiB, 94.23% gc time), 2.609 s (323 allocs: 13.188 KiB), 2.697 s (14 allocs: 272 bytes))\n\nProcessing EPD L2 spectra: Julia is about 100 times faster than Python for spectral derivations across the same interval.\n\ntrange = (\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\nnflux_para = epd_spectral(trange).para\npy_nflux_para = PySPEDAS.elfin.epd(trange; level = \"l2\").ela_pef_hs_nflux_para\n@assert nflux_para ≈ Array(py_nflux_para)'\nb1 = @b epd_spectral($trange)\nb2 = @b PySPEDAS.elfin.epd($trange; level = \"l2\")\n@info \"Julia\" b1\n@info \"PySPEDAS\" b2\n14-Oct-26 19:31:58: ELFIN EPD: START LOADING.\n14-Oct-26 19:31:58: Downloading remote index: https://data.elfin.ucla.edu/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/\n14-Oct-26 19:31:59: Downloading https://data.elfin.ucla.edu/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/ela_l2_epdef_20201001_v01.cdf to elfin_data/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/ela_l2_epdef_20201001_v01.cdf\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: Download of elfin_data/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/ela_l2_epdef_20201001_v01.cdf complete, 9.063 MB in 0.6 sec (14.167 MB/sec) (transfer_normal)\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: Floating point data values for variable ela_pef_Tspin are all fillval (-1.280000e+02)\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: Variable ela_pef_hs_epa_spec DEPEND_1 attribute ela_pef_energies_mean has length 16, but corresponding data dimension has length 10. Removing attribute.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: Variable ela_pef_fs_epa_spec DEPEND_1 attribute ela_pef_energies_mean has length 16, but corresponding data dimension has length 18. Removing attribute.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: store_data: ela_pef_Tspin has empty y component, cannot create variable\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: time_clip: No valid tplot variables matching ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: ELFIN EPD: LOADING END.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: ELFIN EPD L2: START PROCESSING.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: ELFIN EPD L2: START ENERGY SPECTOGRAM.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: ELFIN EPD L2: START PITCH ANGLE SPECTOGRAM.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:00: Energy channel [(0, 2), (3, 5), (6, 8), (9, 15)] are used for epd l2 pitch angle spectra.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:01: ELFIN EPD: START LOADING.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:01: Downloading remote index: https://data.elfin.ucla.edu/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: File is current: elfin_data/ela/l2/epd/fast/electron/2020/ela_l2_epdef_20201001_v01.cdf\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: Floating point data values for variable ela_pef_Tspin are all fillval (-1.280000e+02)\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: Variable ela_pef_hs_epa_spec DEPEND_1 attribute ela_pef_energies_mean has length 16, but corresponding data dimension has length 10. Removing attribute.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: Variable ela_pef_fs_epa_spec DEPEND_1 attribute ela_pef_energies_mean has length 16, but corresponding data dimension has length 18. Removing attribute.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: store_data: ela_pef_Tspin has empty y component, cannot create variable\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: wildcard_expand: No match found for ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: time_clip: No valid tplot variables matching ela_pef_Tspin\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: ELFIN EPD: LOADING END.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: ELFIN EPD L2: START PROCESSING.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: ELFIN EPD L2: START ENERGY SPECTOGRAM.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: ELFIN EPD L2: START PITCH ANGLE SPECTOGRAM.\n14-Oct-26 19:32:02: Energy channel [(0, 2), (3, 5), (6, 8), (9, 15)] are used for epd l2 pitch angle spectra.\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m┌ \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[36m\u001b[1mInfo: \u001b[22m\u001b[39mJulia\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m└ \u001b[22m\u001b[39m  b1 = 1.028 ms (5378 allocs: 3.159 MiB)\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m┌ \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[36m\u001b[1mInfo: \u001b[22m\u001b[39mPySPEDAS\n\u001b[36m\u001b[1m└ \u001b[22m\u001b[39m  b2 = 1.443 s (332 allocs: 14.016 KiB, without a warmup)\n\nnote: Array layout\nJulia arrays follow the column-major convention used by most CDF files (time is the last dimension), whereas NumPy and PySPEDAS use row-major arrays (time is the first dimension). Transpose the PySPEDAS output before comparing so the dimensions align.","title":"Validation and Benchmark with PySPEDAS"},{"category":"section","location":"#ELFINData","page":"Home","text":"(Image: DOI)\n\nLoad and process data from the Electron Losses and Fields Investigation (ELFIN) mission.\n\nReferences: Website, NASA Science, Wikipedia, DOI","title":"ELFINData"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quickstart","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg; Pkg.add(\"ELFINData\")\nusing ELFINData\n\n# Instruments are registries of datasets, selected by keyword\nEPD[probe = \"ela\", level = \"l2\"]                      # Energetic Particle Detector\nFGM[probe = \"ela\", datatype = \"survey\"]               # Fluxgate Magnetometer\nSTATE[probe = \"ela\"]                                  # Spacecraft state/position\n\ntrange = (\"2020-10-01\", \"2020-10-02\")\n\n# EPD L2 spectra: DimStack of omni/para/anti/perp/prec (Energy × Time)\nspectra = epd_spectral(trange)\nspectra.para\nspectra.omni[:, 1]\n\n# Precipitating-to-trapped flux ratio (prec ./ perp)\nratio = ELFINData.flux_ratio(spectra)\n\n# EPD science zone start/end times: (; tstart, tend)\nzones = science_zones(\"ela\")\n\n# Documented EPD data-quality issues overlapping an interval (empty when clean)\nepd_data_notes(\"ela\", \"2022-04-01\", \"2022-04-02\")\n\n# Datasets and variables load with `getdata(x, t0, t1)` or by calling `x(t0, t1)`\nds = ELA_L1_EPDEF(trange)   # CDFDataset\nds[\"ela_pef\"]               # raw counts per sector\nfgs = ELA_FGS(trange)       # CDFVariable (lazy, DimArray-like)\n\n# Time filtering (DimensionalData.jl)\nusing DimensionalData, Dates\nspectra[Ti(DateTime(\"2020-10-01T06:00\") .. DateTime(\"2020-10-01T07:00\"))]","title":"Quickstart"},{"category":"section","location":"#Key-conventions","page":"Home","text":"Time is the last dimension\nProbe is \"ela\" or \"elb\"\nEPD has an electron head (50 keV–5 MeV) and an ion head (50–5000 keV); 16 log-spaced energy channels, mean energies ~63–6500 keV\nOnly FILLVAL reads as NaN: ELFIN files carry placeholder VALIDMIN/VALIDMAX (e.g. 0..1e6 on EPD fluxes, which exceed it), so those bounds are not applied","title":"Key conventions"},{"category":"section","location":"#API","page":"Home","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"section","location":"#Functions","page":"Home","text":"epd_spectral(t0, t1; probe = \"ela\", type = \"nflux\", datatype = \"epdef\", fullspin = false, PAspectra = nothing): type is \"nflux\" or \"eflux\"; fullspin selects full- over half-spin resolution; Espectra keywords pass to VelocityDistributionFunctions.directional_energy_spectra. With PAspectra a NamedTuple, it instead returns a NamedTuple of the energy spectra, pitch-angle spectra ch0, ch1, …, energies, times and pitch_angles; each is the energy-width-weighted mean over energybins = [(1, 3), (4, 6)] (channel indices) or energies = [(50, 160), (160, 345)] (keV), defaulting to channels 1–3, 4–6, 7–9, 10–16.\nscience_zones(probe = \"ela\"): EPD science zone times from the probe's epd_science_zone_times.csv.\nepd_data_notes(probe, t0, t1; head = \"e\"): entries of EPD_DATA_NOTES (from https://elfin.igpp.ucla.edu/data-notes) for head \"e\" (electron) or \"i\" (ion) overlapping [t0, t1).","title":"Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Instruments","page":"Home","text":"Registry Selectors (default first)\nEPD probe, level (\"l1\", \"l2\"), datatype (\"epdef\", \"epdif\"; ion is L1 only)\nFGM probe, datatype (\"survey\", \"fast\")\nSTATE probe","title":"Instruments"},{"category":"section","location":"#Dataset-constants","page":"Home","text":"Constant Contents\nELA_L1_EPDEF / ELB_L1_EPDEF L1 electron counts\nELA_L1_EPDIF / ELB_L1_EPDIF L1 ion counts\nELA_L2_EPDEF / ELB_L2_EPDEF L2 electron flux (calibrated, pitch-angle resolved)\nELA_L1_FGS / ELB_L1_FGS L1 magnetometer, survey mode\nELA_L1_FGF / ELB_L1_FGF L1 magnetometer, fast survey mode\nELA_L1_MRMA / ELB_L1_MRMA L1 MRM data collected by the ACB\nELA_L1_MRMI / ELB_L1_MRMI L1 MRM data collected by the IDPU\nELA_L1_STATE / ELB_L1_STATE L1 spacecraft state","title":"Dataset constants"},{"category":"section","location":"#Variable-constants","page":"Home","text":"Constant Contents\nELA_PEF / ELB_PEF Electron counts per sector (L1, raw)\nELA_PIF / ELB_PIF Ion counts per sector (L1, raw)\nELA_FGS / ELB_FGS B field, sensor XYZ, survey mode;\nELA_POS_GEI / ELB_POS_GEI Spacecraft position (km, GEI)\nELA_MRMA / ELB_MRMA MRM B field (ADC units), sensor XYZ\nELA_MRMI / ELB_MRMI MRM B field (ADC units), sensor XYZ\n\nL2 energy–pitch-angle–time spectra: EL{A,B}_PEF_{HS,FS}_EPAT_{NFLUX,EFLUX} (half/full spin resolution, number/energy flux).","title":"Variable constants"},{"category":"section","location":"#Elsewhere","page":"Home","text":"PySPEDAS (GitHub)","title":"Elsewhere"}]
